"""
A sign-in by an e-mailed code, for the hosted pages of the tenant the request's
host names. Two steps: `requestSignInCode`, then `verifySignInCode`.
"""
type SignInChallenge {
  """
  A secret that goes back with the code. Keep it where the next request
  presents it (the hosted page's server session or a short-lived cookie of its
  own), never in a URL or a log. It is minted for every address, known or not.
  """
  challenge: String!
  "The challenge, and the code with it, can be verified until then."
  expiresAt: DateTime!
}

"The user a session belongs to, in the tenant's own user pool."
type CurrentUser {
  id: ID!
  email: EmailAddress!
  name: String
  emailVerified: Boolean!
}

"A sign-in that opened a session; the session cookie is set on the response."
type SignedIn {
  user: CurrentUser!
  "When the session lapses if not used again; it slides."
  expiresAt: DateTime!
}

"""
A sign-in that is not finished: the user holds a TOTP second factor, so no
session is open yet. Answer it with `confirmSecondFactor` (the app's code),
`recoverSecondFactor` (a recovery code) or `confirmSecondFactorWithPasskey` (its
`passkeyOptions`' answer), with the same `challenge`. The
challenge is a secret like a session token: keep it where the next request
presents it, never in a URL or a log. Single use and `Cache-Control: no-store`.
"""
type SecondFactorChallenge {
  challenge: String!
  "The challenge lapses then."
  expiresAt: DateTime!
  "What can answer it: `totp` always, `passkey` when the user holds one."
  methods: [String!]!
  "JSON text for `navigator.credentials.get({ publicKey })`; present exactly when `methods` holds `passkey`."
  passkeyOptions: String
  "The path a social flow was started with, or null (always null for a code or a link)."
  returnTo: String
}

"What a sign-in by code or link answers: a session, or a second-factor challenge to answer first."
union SignInResult = SignedIn | SecondFactorChallenge

"""
The answer to `requestMagicLink`: always the same, whether the address has an
account or not, so it says nothing about it. The link itself only reaches the
inbox.
"""
type MagicLinkRequested {
  "The link lives until then (15 minutes); only the last link sent works."
  expiresAt: DateTime!
}

type Query {
  "The signed-in user of this tenant, or null for an anonymous request."
  currentUser: CurrentUser
}

type Mutation {
  """
  Asks for a six-digit code by e-mail. The answer is the same for an address
  with an account, one without and, on a tenant that closed sign-up, one that
  is not invited: a code is sent only when an account exists (or sign-up is
  open). Errors: MAIL_THROTTLED (429) past five requests per address and ten
  minutes; SSO_REQUIRED (403) for an address whose domain requires single
  sign-on (`hostedHomeRealm` names the connection to use).
  """
  requestSignInCode(email: EmailAddress!): SignInChallenge!
  """
  Checks the code against its challenge and opens the session, or, for a user
  who holds a TOTP second factor, answers a `SecondFactorChallenge` (no session
  yet). Every refusal (wrong, spent, expired or unknown challenge) is the same
  CODE_INVALID, 401. SSO_REQUIRED (403), with no session, when the user's
  domain requires single sign-on.
  """
  verifySignInCode(challenge: String!, code: String!): SignInResult!
  """
  Asks for a sign-in link by e-mail (only when the deployment turns magic-link
  sign-in on; otherwise 404 MAGIC_LINK_DISABLED, as if the operation did not
  exist). The answer is the same for an address with an account, one without
  and, on a tenant that closed sign-up, one that is not invited. The link opens
  the hosted page `/sign-in/link?token=...` of the tenant, which must POST the
  token to `confirmMagicLink` (never sign in on GET: mail scanners open links).
  Errors: MAGIC_LINK_DISABLED (404), MAIL_THROTTLED (429), SSO_REQUIRED (403)
  for an address whose domain requires single sign-on.
  """
  requestMagicLink(email: EmailAddress!): MagicLinkRequested!
  """
  Redeems the token of a sign-in link, proves the address and opens the session
  (the cookie is set on the response). Every refusal (unknown, spent, expired or
  stale link, deactivated user) is the same MAGIC_LINK_INVALID, 401; the page
  offers a new link. MAGIC_LINK_DISABLED (404) when the switch is off; the token
  is not spent then. SSO_REQUIRED (403), with no session, when the user's
  domain requires single sign-on.
  """
  confirmMagicLink(token: String!): SignInResult!
  """
  Mails the signed-in user a link that proves their address (hosted page
  `/verify?token=...`, which must POST the token to `confirmEmailVerification`,
  never confirm on GET). Always true: an already verified user gets the same
  answer and no mail. Errors: UNAUTHENTICATED (401), TENANT_SUSPENDED (403),
  EMAIL_VERIFICATION_THROTTLED (429, `retryAfter` and `Retry-After`).
  """
  requestEmailVerification: Boolean!
  """
  Redeems the token of a verification link for the signed-in account only and
  returns it with `emailVerified: true`. Every refusal (unknown, spent, expired
  or stale token, another account's token, which is left unspent) is the same
  EMAIL_VERIFICATION_INVALID, 400; the page offers a new link. UNAUTHENTICATED
  (401) without a session, TENANT_SUSPENDED (403).
  """
  confirmEmailVerification(token: String!): CurrentUser!
  "Ends the session of the request and clears the cookie. True even when anonymous."
  signOut: Boolean!
}
